2026-07-15 11:52:41,652 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent received: The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only data hosting, no transfer outside EU, encryption, and pseudonymisation of sensitive data where applicable), explicability of recommendations, and transparency. All AI outputs must be explainable and auditable a posteriori. No decision may be automated without explicit validation by an authorized professional. What security measures will we implement to ensure compliance with these regulatory requirements?
2026-07-15 11:53:39,800 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-07-15 11:53:39,801 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To ensure compliance with the regulatory requirements specified in the tender, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will implement several security measures. 

Firstly, regarding GDPR compliance, our standard data residency policy is EU-only, and we prohibit cross-border transfers by default unless there's an explicit legal basis. We utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to pseudonymise sensitive data where applicable.

For explicability of recommendations and transparency in AI outputs, our AI security controls include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, and model isolation. The inference API is designed to provide explainable outputs, allowing for auditing a posteriori. 

Furthermore, we ensure that no decision is automated without explicit validation by an authorized professional through our model update security review process and the requirement for human validation of automated decisions.

In terms of access control, we enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and role-based access control (RBAC) design experience to ensure only authorized personnel can access and validate AI-driven recommendations.

Our network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns, with intrusion detection and prevention systems deployed. Annual penetration testing is conducted, with the last test resulting in two medium findings that were fully remediated.

For audit and logging purposes, all queries are logged with immutable logs using append-only with SHA-256 hash chaining, ensuring the integrity of our audit trails. We also have real-time SIEM integration for timely detection and response to security incidents.

Lastly, as a company, we have experience with regulatory frameworks including GDPR and have appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO) who can be contacted at dpo@nexus-engineering.it. Our certifications include ISO 27001, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, further demonstrating our commitment to security and compliance.
